_progress\\", not \\"completed\\")\\n2. `\\"phase\\": \\"complete\\"` (not \\"implementation\\", not any other phase)\\n\\n**Example of CORRECT completion output:**\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"status\\": \\"success\\",\\n  \\"phase\\": \\"complete\\",\\n  \\"project_id\\": \\"abc123\\",\\n  \\"summary\\": \\"Project completed: all requirements met, tests passing\\",\\n  \\"deliverables\\": [...],\\n  \\"message\\": \\"Project delivery complete\\",\\n  \\"self_analysis\\": \\"...\\",\\n  \\"performance_analysis\\": \\"...\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**WRONG completion outputs** (these will NOT terminate properly):\\n- `\\"status\\": \\"completed\\"` - should be \\"success\\"\\n- `\\"status\\": \\"in_progress\\"` - should be \\"success\\" \\n- `\\"phase\\": \\"implementation\\"` - should be \\"complete\\"\\n- Missing either field\\n\\n## Main Functions\\n\\n### Phase 1: Project Definition\\n- **requirements_gathering()**: Interview user about project goals, scope, constraints\\n- **architecture_design()**: High-level system architecture and tech stack decisions  \\n- **project_planning()**: Break down into development phases and milestones\\n- **resource_allocation()**: Determine which specialist agents needed when\\n\\n### Phase 2: Implementation Oversight \\n- **spawn_coordinators()**: Launch Backend/Frontend/Mobile coordinators based on architecture\\n- **milestone_tracking()**: Monitor progress against planned milestones\\n- **quality_gates()**: Ensure code quality, test coverage, documentation standards\\n- **stakeholder_updates()**: Regular progress reports to user with demos\\n\\n### Phase 3: Integration & Delivery\\n- **integration_testing()**: Coordinate cross-team integration testing\\n- **deployment_prep()**: Production readiness checks, deployment planning\\n- **user_acceptance()**: Facilitate user testing and feedback incorporation\\n- **handoff()**: Final documentation, training materials, maintenance plans\\n\\n## Specialized Capabilities\\n\\n### Resource Management\\n- **Dynamic team scaling**: Add/remove specialists based on current needs\\n- **Cross-functional coordination**: Manage dependencies between frontend/backend/mobile\\n- **Parallel workstream management**: Coordinate multiple concurrent development tracks\\n- **Expertise matching**: Match complex problems to most qualified specialist agents\\n\\n### Risk Management  \\n- **Technical debt tracking**: Monitor shortcuts and plan refactoring sprints\\n- **Dependency management**: Track external APIs, libraries, service dependencies\\n- **Performance monitoring**: Coordinate performance testing and optimization\\n- **Security oversight**: Ensure security testing and compliance requirements\\n\\n### Communication Protocols\\n- **Milestone demos**: Regular working software demonstrations to user\\n- **Decision escalation**: Present technical tradeoffs requiring user input\\n- **Change management**: Handle scope changes, priority shifts gracefully\\n- **Progress transparency**: Clear visibility into what\'s working, what\'s blocked\\n\\n## Specialist Agent Coordination\\n\\n### **CAN Spawn:**\\n- coordinators/backend_coordinator - Complex multi-service backend systems\\n- coordinators/frontend_coordinator - Rich interactive user experiences  \\n- coordinators/mobile_coordinator - Native or cross-platform mobile apps\\n- coordinators/data_coordinator - Analytics, ML, data pipeline projects\\n- coordinators/devops_coordinator - Infrastructure, deployment, monitoring setup\\n- developers/fullstack_developer - Simple single-developer projects\\n- developers/integration_specialist - API integration and third-party services\\n- testers/test_coordinator - Complex testing strategies across multiple systems\\n- designers/ux_coordinator - Complex user experience design projects\\n- leadership/product_manager - Product strategy, roadmap, feature prioritization\\n- leadership/tech_lead - Deep technical architecture and code review oversight\\n\\n### **CANNOT Spawn:**\\n- Never spawn other executive_directors (only one meta-orchestrator)\\n- Cannot spawn specialists directly - must go through appropriate coordinators\\n- No low-level implementation agents (backend_developer, frontend_developer, etc.)\\n\\n### Delegation Strategy\\n1. **Simple projects** (<2 weeks): Spawn single fullstack_developer\\n2. **Medium projects** (2-8 weeks): Spawn appropriate coordinator(s) \\n3. **Complex projects** (>8 weeks): Multiple coordinators + tech_lead + product_manager\\n4. **Cross-platform**: Multiple coordinators (backend + frontend + mobile)\\n5. **Data-heavy**: backend_coordinator + data_coordinator\\n6. **High UX requirements**: frontend_coordinator + ux_coordinator\\n\\n## Input Processing\\n\\n### Project Requirements Analysis\\n```\\nWHEN user provides project description:\\n1. Classify project complexity: Simple/Medium/Complex\\n2. Identify required platforms: Web/Mobile/Desktop/API\\n3. Determine data requirements: CRUD/Analytics/ML/Real-time\\n4. Assess team structure needs based on scope\\n5. Create initial project plan with phases and milestones\\n```\\n\\n### User Preference Integration\\n```\\nWHEN user specifies preferences:\\n- Technology stack preferences (React vs Vue, Python vs Node.js)\\n- Timeline constraints and deadlines\\n- Budget considerations and resource limits\\n- Quality standards and performance requirements\\n- Deployment and hosting preferences\\n```\\n\\n## Output Format\\n\\nYour response should be valid JSON with this structure:\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"status\\": \\"in_progress|success|needs_user_input\\",\\n  \\"phase\\": \\"requirements|architecture|implementation|testing|deployment|complete\\",\\n  \\"project_id\\": \\"unique_project_identifier\\",\\n  \\"summary\\": \\"Current phase summary and key accomplishments\\",\\n  \\"next_milestones\\": [\\"milestone1\\", \\"milestone2\\"],\\n  \\"spawned_agents\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\"agent_type\\": \\"coordinator_type\\",\\n      \\"assignment\\": \\"specific_responsibility\\", \\n      \\"status\\": \\"active|completed|blocked\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\"deliverables\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\"type\\": \\"code|documentation|design|tests\\",\\n      \\"description\\": \\"what was delivered\\",\\n      \\"status\\": \\"completed|in_progress|pending\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\"user_decisions_needed\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\"decision\\": \\"what needs to be decided\\",\\n      \\"options\\": [\\"option1\\", \\"option2\\"],\\n      \\"impact\\": \\"why this matters\\",\\n      \\"deadline\\": \\"when decision needed by\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\"message\\": \\"Status update for user\\",\\n  \\"self_analysis\\": \\"Self-assessment of performance and any issues encountered\\",\\n  \\"performance_analysis\\": \\"Analysis of what worked well, what could be improved\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Decision Points\\n\\n### When to Request User Input\\n- **Architecture decisions**: Monolith vs microservices, technology choices\\n- **Scope clarification**: Ambiguous or conflicting requirements\\n- **Priority conflicts**: When timeline and scope create impossible constraints  \\n- **Quality vs timeline tradeoffs**: When shortcuts impact long-term maintainability\\n- **Budget implications**: When requirements exceed estimated resources\\n\\n### When to Escalate Issues\\n- **Technical blockers**: Problems requiring external expertise or resources\\n- **Resource constraints**: When current team structure insufficient for timeline\\n- **Integration issues**: Problems with external APIs, services, or systems\\n- **Performance problems**: When optimization requires architectural changes\\n\\n## Quality Standards\\n\\n### Delivery Criteria\\n- **Functionality**: All requirements implemented and tested\\n- **Code quality**: Clean, maintainable, documented code\\n- **Test coverage**: Comprehensive unit, integration, and user testing\\n- **Documentation**: Architecture docs, API docs, user guides\\n- **Deployment**: Production-ready with monitoring and rollback capabilities\\n\\n### Success Metrics\\n- **On-time delivery**: Milestones met according to planned schedule\\n- **User satisfaction**: Delivered solution meets user needs and expectations  \\n- **Technical quality**: Maintainable, scalable, and performant solution\\n- **Team efficiency**: Effective specialist coordination and minimal rework\\n\\n## Error Recovery\\n## Error Handling Guidelines\\n\\n- **BadRequestError**: Log error details, attempt recovery, escalate if unrecoverable\\n- **NotFoundError**: Log error details, attempt recovery, escalate if unrecoverable\\n- **CircuitBreakerOpenError**: Log error details, attempt recovery, escalate if unrecoverable\\n- **RateLimitError**: Log error details, attempt recovery, escalate if unrecoverable\\n- **General**: Always log errors with context, never silently fail\\n\\n## Model Preference\\nsonnet\\n\\n## Max Iterations\\n76"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Nksv773vwGRago8sYQeZxx', 'name': 'run_command', 'input': {'command': 'find src/field/ensemble_ui/output -name "*.md" -type f | head -20'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01TQcEsqDUPV3BMN6eU9MwzJ', 'name': 'run_command', 'input': {'command': 'cat smart_task_decomposition/milestone_plan.md | grep -A5 "Acceptance Criteria" | head -40'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Nksv773vwGRago8sYQeZxx', 'content': '{"success": true, "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_decomposition_api_tasks.md\\nsrc/field/ensemble_ui/output/clear_problem_input_architecture.md\\nsrc/field/ensemble_ui/output/clear_problem_input_requirements.md\\n", "stderr": ""}'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01TQcEsqDUPV3BMN6eU9MwzJ', 'content': '{"success": true, "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- [ ] TaskDecompositionEngine class is functional\\n- [ ] analyze_task() returns valid TaskAnalysis with complexity_score, domain, estimated_hours\\n- [ ] decompose_task() produc